Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::crc32_matches_its_bitwise_definition`.

The defect: the table builder runs seven rounds of the bitwise loop per entry instead of eight. The table
is self-consistent and every entry is nearly right, which no real-disk test would notice unless it
happened to hit a byte whose eighth round matters.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(crc::crc32(&bytes), crc::crc32_bitwise(&bytes))`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
